Multiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\sqrt{7}-\sqrt{2}$.
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{\sqrt{7}-\sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{7}+\sqrt{2}}&=\frac{(\sqrt{7}-\sqrt{2})^2}{(\sqrt{7}+\sqrt{2})(\sqrt{7}-\sqrt{2})}\\
\frac{\sqrt{7}-\sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{7}+\sqrt{2}}&=\frac{7-2\sqrt{14}+2}{7-2}\\
\frac{\sqrt{7}-\sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{7}+\sqrt{2}}&=\frac{9-2\sqrt{14}}{5}
\end{align*}$$

Multiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate $3\sqrt{3}+5$.
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{3\sqrt{3}+5}{3\sqrt{3}-5}&=\frac{(3\sqrt{3}+5)^2}{(3\sqrt{3}-5)(3\sqrt{3}+5)}\\
\frac{3\sqrt{3}+5}{3\sqrt{3}-5}&=\frac{27+30\sqrt{3}+25}{27-25}\\
\frac{3\sqrt{3}+5}{3\sqrt{3}-5}&=26+15\sqrt{3}
\end{align*}$$

$$\begin{align*}
\frac{2}{6-3\sqrt{3}}&=\frac{2(6+3\sqrt{3})}{(6-3\sqrt{3})(6+3\sqrt{3})}\\
\frac{2}{6-3\sqrt{3}}&=\frac{12+6\sqrt{3}}{36-27}\\
\frac{2}{6-3\sqrt{3}}&=\frac{4+2\sqrt{3}}{3}
\end{align*}$$
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{2\sqrt{3}+3}&=\frac{2\sqrt{3}-3}{(2\sqrt{3}+3)(2\sqrt{3}-3)}\\
\frac{1}{2\sqrt{3}+3}&=\frac{2\sqrt{3}-3}{12-9}\\
\frac{1}{2\sqrt{3}+3}&=\frac{2\sqrt{3}-3}{3}
\end{align*}$$
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{2}{6-3\sqrt{3}}-\frac{1}{2\sqrt{3}+3}&=\frac{4+2\sqrt{3}-(2\sqrt{3}-3)}{3}\\
\frac{2}{6-3\sqrt{3}}-\frac{1}{2\sqrt{3}+3}&=\frac{7}{3}
\end{align*}$$
Since $7$ and $3$ are integers and $3\ne0$, the result is rational.
